The grip pass is render-bound rather than compute-bound because it is producing all requested close-ups against the dense groom. The first clips are progressing without assertion failures; each audit checks the actual evaluated sword tip, every quarter-frame hilt transform, and the repaired closed-finger mesh—not just the animation channels. I’m keeping the full requested close-up set rather than reducing evidence frames.
