codex
The dedicated head/groom/collar pass is now evaluating every integer frame. It verifies the eyebrow and groom control weights/modifier targets, checks the visible native curves’ control chain, measures blade clearance against the head and sampled groom controls, and runs triangle-overlap tests between the MPFB head/neck surface and the gorget/rim. This is the heaviest non-render check because it rebuilds posed surface acceleration structures frame by frame.
