The collision probe found a clean, minimal control solution: a temporary neck yaw away from the blade clears the head without moving the sword or breaking the arm chain. I’m applying a smooth frame-30-to-62 avoidance arc peaking during the frame-46 passage, which fits the existing 360° spin as a gaze/neck counterturn. Once saved, I’ll verify the full interval—not just the peak—and reject it if the groom, collar, or silhouette introduces a new issue.
