The first avoidance curve cleared the peak but was too gradual: it still clipped at frame 40, brushed groom controls at 38/42–43, and its late fade created one frame of visible collar contact at 54. I’ve narrowed the correction to a full counterturn plateau over frames 38–50 with an earlier ramp and a complete return by 54. The fixer now restores the original neck channels before applying, so reruns are idempotent and do not stack rotations.
