codex
The conservative cylindrical blade proxy was intentionally broad and is now over-reporting groom contact. An exact surface query at the flagged frame shows 95.87 mm of clearance from sampled groom controls to the actual blade after the 2 mm fiber allowance; the proxy’s negative result came from treating the whole sword as a 143 mm-radius cylinder. I’m upgrading the full audit to use the actual blade BVH for both head and groom on rising spin and X-slash. Rising’s exact head surface remains clear, though narrowly—1.45 mm at its closest frame—which will be called out honestly.
